## 6. Demo Flow Verification — All 5 Flows

### Flow 1 — Stock Update (Hindi)
```
User says: "50 relay aaye hain"
→ POST /agent/parse { shop_id: "shop_01", message: "50 relay aaye hain" }
→ Agent: { action: "update_stock", sku: "ELE-OMR-24V", quantity: 50, confidence: 0.90+ }
→ Frontend shows confirmation card
→ User taps Confirm
→ POST /inventory/update { shop_id: "shop_01", sku: "ELE-OMR-24V", quantity: 50, update_type: "incoming" }
→ Toast: "Stock updated!"
```

### Flow 2 — Sale Record
```
User: "5 stepper motor becha 4250 mein"
→ Agent: { action: "record_sale", sku: "MOT-N17-001", qty_sold: 5, amount: 4250.0 }
→ Confirmation card → Confirm
→ POST /sales/record { ... }
→ Inventory auto-deducted
```

### Flow 3 — Khata Check
```
User: "TechNova ka kitna baaki hai"
→ Agent: { action: "khata_payment", customer_name: "TechNova Engineering Works", amount: 0 }
→ Frontend shows ₹45,000 outstanding
```

### Flow 4 — Analytics Report
```
User: "aaj ka report dikhao"
→ Agent: { action: "unknown", response_text: "Here is today's summary..." }
→ Frontend navigates to Reports tab / shows summary
```

### Flow 5 — Low-Confidence Clarification
```
User: "thoda soap order karo"
→ Agent: { action: "unknown", confidence: 0.3, response_text: "Kitna soap chahiye? Please exact number batayein." }
→ No confirmation card (confidence < 0.7)
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Flow 4 (reports) requires a new action type in the backend OR frontend-side handling to navigate to the reports tab when the intent is a report request. Simplest fix: frontend checks if `response_text` mentions "report" and auto-opens the reports tab.

